WEBVTT

00:00:11.050 --> 00:00:13.590
"April 14th - 7:00 AM"

00:00:13.590 --> 00:00:16.010
"A Southwestern Republic of UZSR
City of Borshev"

00:00:45.920 --> 00:00:52.420
"Irina: The Vampire Cosmonaut"

00:02:04.160 --> 00:02:10.210
Nearly 200,000 people gather
to see the world's first cosmonaut.

00:02:10.210 --> 00:02:13.130
The celebration scheduled for 3 PM

00:02:13.130 --> 00:02:18.840
will be the Republic's first simultaneous
live broadcast to the world.

00:02:23.220 --> 00:02:24.930
Remember what to say?

00:02:24.930 --> 00:02:26.020
Yeah.

00:02:26.020 --> 00:02:32.230
Don't mess it up. Three billion people
will be listening on the radio and TV.

00:02:39.360 --> 00:02:46.080
Cosmonaut Major Lev Leps has just
arrived by plane at Sangrad Airport!

00:02:46.080 --> 00:02:47.910
It's Major Lev Leps!

00:02:53.000 --> 00:02:55.460
Major Leps is coming down the ramp!

00:02:56.460 --> 00:02:59.510
He has just reached the ground!

00:02:59.510 --> 00:03:03.220
"Sangrad Airport"
He's being welcomed by a huge crowd!

00:03:03.680 --> 00:03:09.560
The officers rejoice at their
hero's triumphant return!

00:03:15.770 --> 00:03:18.780
"Sangrad -
National Military Medical Center"

00:03:20.360 --> 00:03:23.660
The military's drugs sure are potent.

00:03:26.990 --> 00:03:28.790
--Let's go.
--Mmm.

00:03:30.500 --> 00:03:34.830
I became the world's first
cosmonaut for our motherland.

00:03:34.830 --> 00:03:36.540
Mmm.

00:03:36.540 --> 00:03:43.510
I'll gladly fulfill my next mission
to further honor our motherland.

00:03:45.680 --> 00:03:47.260
Congratulations.

00:03:56.940 --> 00:03:59.070
Well done, Lev.

00:03:59.070 --> 00:04:00.530
Thank you.

00:04:04.360 --> 00:04:07.370
Look, your parents are waiting.

00:04:09.120 --> 00:04:15.670
I wish to personally thank you
for raising your child into a hero.

00:04:18.170 --> 00:04:21.010
You never told us a thing.

00:04:24.680 --> 00:04:28.010
He's been reunited with his parents!

00:04:28.010 --> 00:04:32.850
Major Leps will soon
depart for Glorious Square!

00:04:38.310 --> 00:04:41.480
"Previous Day - 9:02 PM"
--Escape? Are you serious?!
--Shh!

00:04:41.990 --> 00:04:46.030
Most of the security will be
at the ceremony tomorrow.

00:04:46.030 --> 00:04:49.830
If we sneak into the crowd,
they'll never see us.

00:04:49.830 --> 00:04:52.790
But, if I escape--

00:04:52.790 --> 00:04:56.540
After seeing you and Lev
put your lives on the line,

00:04:56.540 --> 00:04:59.960
I want to do something, too.

00:04:59.960 --> 00:05:02.550
Anya...

00:05:02.550 --> 00:05:07.840
It's your decision. If you want this,
I'll help however I can.

00:05:15.730 --> 00:05:17.400
Are you okay?!

00:05:17.400 --> 00:05:19.230
Yeah, I guess.

00:05:19.230 --> 00:05:22.650
All right. Let's try to hurry.

00:05:22.650 --> 00:05:24.610
--Anya.
--Hmm?

00:05:24.610 --> 00:05:27.450
Why even go this far?

00:05:27.450 --> 00:05:32.950
To make sure it comes true--
your real New Year's wish.

00:05:37.920 --> 00:05:42.130
Yes. We'll seize the experiment
subject at 3:00 as planned.

00:05:52.350 --> 00:05:54.560
Did something bad happen?

00:05:54.560 --> 00:05:55.520
Eh?

00:05:55.520 --> 00:05:58.520
It shows on your face.

00:05:58.520 --> 00:06:01.310
I'm just tired, that's all.

00:06:01.310 --> 00:06:05.610
--You're hiding something, aren't you?
--Not really.

00:06:05.610 --> 00:06:10.570
State secrets? I won't
force you to answer.

00:06:16.290 --> 00:06:19.670
Major Lev Leps, hurrah!

00:06:19.670 --> 00:06:25.670
Your mother and I lived
our entire lives in this country.

00:06:25.670 --> 00:06:31.220
We've lost friends to war
and have seen numerous purges.

00:06:31.220 --> 00:06:35.600
Our motherland disposes
of anything inconvenient.

00:06:35.600 --> 00:06:40.150
It makes truths out of lies
and lies out of truths.

00:06:40.150 --> 00:06:46.740
I wonder, Lev, what do all these
people expect from you?

00:06:47.780 --> 00:06:50.820
--Major, it's time!
--Right.

00:06:50.820 --> 00:06:56.040
You flew through space.
Don't let the country hold you down.

00:06:56.040 --> 00:06:59.160
Soar ahead to a new era.

00:07:28.900 --> 00:07:32.780
Irina!

00:07:32.780 --> 00:07:36.910
Your face is so red! The sun...!

00:07:38.370 --> 00:07:41.960
It's fine. Let's keep going.

00:07:41.960 --> 00:07:47.920
"Sangrad - Glorious Square"
As the world looks on,
Major Lev Leps arrives at the square!

00:07:47.920 --> 00:07:51.800
The hero's celebration is about to begin!

00:07:54.550 --> 00:07:56.850
What happened?

00:07:56.850 --> 00:07:58.640
Unbelievable.

00:08:08.320 --> 00:08:12.320
Irina, there he is! It's Lev!

00:08:12.320 --> 00:08:13.820
Lev...

00:08:18.200 --> 00:08:23.790
We'll now commence the ceremony
for Comrade Lev Leps!

00:08:30.260 --> 00:08:33.430
Irina, let's get in the shade.

00:08:33.430 --> 00:08:38.560
I present: the hero of
Zirnitra Union, Major Lev Leps.

00:08:38.560 --> 00:08:43.140
He will now address his
countrymen and all of humanity.

00:08:47.980 --> 00:08:51.150
My dear comrades...

00:08:51.150 --> 00:08:54.360
My dear Fyodor Gergiev...

00:08:54.360 --> 00:08:58.870
Thank you for letting me,
an ordinary person,

00:08:58.870 --> 00:09:02.660
become the world's first cosmonaut.

00:09:07.040 --> 00:09:11.630
To all the workers
who built the spaceship:

00:09:11.630 --> 00:09:15.510
Not once did I doubt our success.

00:09:15.510 --> 00:09:20.850
"United Kingdom of Arnack"
I believe our marvelous ship
will take us even farther!

00:09:21.100 --> 00:09:23.980
"United Kingdom of Arnack
Dhampir Residential Zone"
Our supremacy in science
will unlock the secrets of space!

00:09:27.480 --> 00:09:30.940
"Lilitto
Capital"
To my fellow candidates who
endured the grueling training:

00:09:33.150 --> 00:09:40.910
Soon, you will take to space and become
the 2nd and 3rd cosmonauts in history.

00:09:40.910 --> 00:09:47.500
The first artificial satellite,
animal spaceflight, manned spaceflight!

00:09:47.500 --> 00:09:50.340
At this moment, I am overjoyed!

00:09:52.590 --> 00:09:55.760
My dear Fyodor Gergiev...

00:09:55.760 --> 00:10:01.930
You were the first to embrace and
congratulate me after flying in space!

00:10:06.810 --> 00:10:09.690
I wanted to congratulate him first.

00:10:09.690 --> 00:10:11.520
Irina...

00:10:11.520 --> 00:10:16.530
I give my thanks to all
the people who supported me!

00:10:16.530 --> 00:10:18.700
Thanks, Anya.

00:10:18.700 --> 00:10:19.740
Huh?

00:10:22.450 --> 00:10:24.490
W-Wait!

00:10:28.920 --> 00:10:31.290
Let's go back together.

00:10:35.630 --> 00:10:38.380
Long live Zirnitra Union!

00:10:38.380 --> 00:10:43.100
Hurrah! Hurrah! Hurrah!

00:10:43.100 --> 00:10:46.060
Long live my dear comrades!

00:10:46.060 --> 00:10:50.060
Hurrah! Hurrah! Hurrah!

00:10:50.060 --> 00:10:51.150
Also...!

00:10:56.740 --> 00:10:58.360
What's wrong?

00:10:58.360 --> 00:11:00.110
He forget his lines?

00:11:21.220 --> 00:11:24.890
What? I see... Got it.

00:11:37.150 --> 00:11:42.030
Sorry. I finally remembered
what I was going to say.

00:11:45.620 --> 00:11:49.910
My dear comrades,
I'd like to correct something:

00:11:49.910 --> 00:11:53.500
I'm not the world's first cosmonaut.

00:11:55.090 --> 00:11:59.550
The first person in space
was a 17-year-old girl.

00:11:59.550 --> 00:12:05.470
Her name: Irina Luminesk.
Not a human, but a vampire!

00:12:10.020 --> 00:12:12.640
Wh-What? You're kidding!

00:12:14.310 --> 00:12:18.820
--This is treason!
--Calm down. No need to panic.

00:12:18.820 --> 00:12:20.030
The hell--?

00:12:20.030 --> 00:12:23.700
Hey, what kind of speech is this?

00:12:23.700 --> 00:12:25.780
An unexpected one.

00:12:25.780 --> 00:12:26.990
Stop him!

00:12:26.990 --> 00:12:32.830
Impossible--he's a hero.
How would you explain it to the world?

00:12:34.000 --> 00:12:38.670
Just let him continue.
We'll make excuses later.

00:12:38.670 --> 00:12:46.140
Irina went to space to test the effects
of zero-G and the safety of the spaceship.

00:12:46.140 --> 00:12:50.390
She's the reason I could come home safely.

00:12:50.390 --> 00:12:54.480
Unfortunately, she couldn't be here today.

00:12:54.480 --> 00:12:56.020
Lev...!

00:12:56.020 --> 00:12:59.860
She's probably hiding
from the sun somewhere.

00:13:02.530 --> 00:13:08.030
Do you hate vampires for being
a "cursed species"?

00:13:08.030 --> 00:13:10.490
I'll be honest.

00:13:10.490 --> 00:13:16.460
Much like all of you, I believed vampires
were to be loathed and feared.

00:13:16.460 --> 00:13:21.130
That's absurd. None of it is true.

00:13:21.130 --> 00:13:26.680
She's in no way different
than my friends or family.

00:13:29.930 --> 00:13:31.220
Irina!

00:13:33.270 --> 00:13:42.690
She's just a sweet girl who has her own
dreams and yearns for the stars.

00:13:42.690 --> 00:13:48.570
She loves lemon seltzer,
gets drunk with a sip of <i>zhizni</i>,

00:13:48.570 --> 00:13:51.790
and makes delicious <i>kholodets</i>.

00:13:51.790 --> 00:13:57.250
She conquered her fear of heights,
likes jazz and ice skating,

00:13:57.250 --> 00:14:00.670
--and yelled watching her first movie.
--Please, set already!

00:14:00.670 --> 00:14:05.920
--This girl, like you and me...
--Hey you! Stop!

00:14:05.920 --> 00:14:10.180
...is another person on this planet.

00:14:10.180 --> 00:14:18.770
Know that this girl, confined to solitude,
reached space before anyone else!

00:14:18.770 --> 00:14:21.860
--People of the world, honor her!
--Stay away!

00:14:21.860 --> 00:14:24.070
Behave yourself, girl.

00:14:24.070 --> 00:14:26.030
--Irina!
--Huh?

00:14:26.030 --> 00:14:27.700
Stop!

00:14:27.700 --> 00:14:28.910
What?!

00:14:30.910 --> 00:14:33.280
Irina! Go!

00:14:33.280 --> 00:14:35.700
Mmm!

00:14:35.700 --> 00:14:39.460
This was the second cosmonaut, Lev Leps!

00:14:39.460 --> 00:14:41.580
Lev!

00:14:44.710 --> 00:14:46.090
Irina!

00:14:46.090 --> 00:14:48.680
Don't shoot! Wait for orders!

00:14:48.680 --> 00:14:50.180
Irina!

00:14:50.180 --> 00:14:52.180
That way! The stairs!

00:14:52.180 --> 00:14:53.600
Mmm!

00:15:14.530 --> 00:15:15.990
Lev!

00:15:15.990 --> 00:15:17.620
Irina!

00:15:34.350 --> 00:15:36.850
Um, Lev...

00:15:36.850 --> 00:15:38.850
You surprised me.

00:15:41.020 --> 00:15:43.980
Let's introduce you to everyone.

00:15:47.360 --> 00:15:50.900
Everyone, this is the girl I spoke of:

00:15:50.900 --> 00:15:55.620
Irina Luminesk,
the world's first cosmonaut.

00:15:55.620 --> 00:15:57.200
That's a real vampire?

00:15:57.200 --> 00:15:59.410
--Disguised as human?
--Filthy!

00:15:59.410 --> 00:16:02.250
--We'll be cursed!
--A monster went to space?

00:16:02.250 --> 00:16:04.170
Go ahead, Irina.

00:16:04.170 --> 00:16:05.380
Huh?

00:16:05.380 --> 00:16:09.300
Introduce yourself as a cosmonaut.

00:16:09.300 --> 00:16:10.920
Unbelievable!

00:16:13.970 --> 00:16:19.220
Be proud of yourself.
You've done incredible things.

00:16:21.850 --> 00:16:25.730
Didn't you realize something
seeing the moon?

00:16:25.730 --> 00:16:30.030
You were going to say
something on the plains.

00:16:30.030 --> 00:16:33.030
Why not share that with everyone?

00:16:33.030 --> 00:16:37.490
That day... What I wanted to say...

00:16:49.460 --> 00:16:51.840
Lev, I'm fine now.

00:16:56.850 --> 00:16:59.680
I am Irina Luminesk.

00:16:59.680 --> 00:17:01.520
Get lost, vampire!

00:17:01.520 --> 00:17:07.770
Seeing the world from space
was incredibly beautiful, um...

00:17:07.770 --> 00:17:15.160
I always wanted to go to space--
to go there before humans did.

00:17:15.160 --> 00:17:16.870
Go home, monster!

00:17:16.870 --> 00:17:18.830
--Yeah!
--Yeah!

00:17:30.380 --> 00:17:35.260
I hated humans. I resented them.

00:17:36.630 --> 00:17:40.640
--You devil!
--It's her true colors!
--Kill her!

00:17:40.640 --> 00:17:45.690
I thought all humans deserved to die.

00:17:45.690 --> 00:17:52.230
And though I was like that,
Lev here made me into a cosmonaut.

00:17:52.230 --> 00:17:57.700
He made my dream come true!
And now, my new dream is...

00:18:03.160 --> 00:18:10.340
...to go to the moon with him! This was
Irina Luminesk, cosmonaut of Lilitto!

00:18:32.320 --> 00:18:34.860
Wonderful!

00:18:34.860 --> 00:18:38.360
Wonderful speech! Thank you!

00:18:38.360 --> 00:18:40.950
Thank you for all you've done!

00:19:05.850 --> 00:19:13.270
My dear comrades! The actions
of Lev Leps and Irina Luminesk

00:19:13.270 --> 00:19:15.860
shall forever be praised!

00:19:20.320 --> 00:19:23.870
Now then, I'd like to apologize.

00:19:23.870 --> 00:19:30.250
A few issues arose before
this worldwide live broadcast.

00:19:30.250 --> 00:19:37.130
As a result, Comrade Luminesk
arrived late and this confusion ensued.

00:19:38.840 --> 00:19:43.970
Said trouble was caused by
the so-called "Delivery Crew."

00:19:43.970 --> 00:19:47.720
They wanted to kill this vampire.

00:19:47.720 --> 00:19:54.400
However, are we to stand by
and let our neighbors be killed?

00:19:54.400 --> 00:19:58.440
No! Purges are a thing of the past!

00:19:58.440 --> 00:20:06.740
Furthermore, countries that discriminate
and exploit dhampir are behind the times!

00:20:06.740 --> 00:20:09.540
This is outdated thinking!

00:20:09.540 --> 00:20:17.000
In our progressive country, even the
dreams of vampires can come true!

00:20:17.000 --> 00:20:21.680
--Long live Zirnitra Union!
--Long live Zirnitra Union!

00:20:21.680 --> 00:20:27.180
What was that? It's like you
planned for me to reveal everything.

00:20:27.180 --> 00:20:29.770
I did.

00:20:29.770 --> 00:20:32.850
We prepared two statements.

00:20:32.850 --> 00:20:39.530
If you hadn't said anything, we wouldn't
have criticized the UK or Delivery Crew.

00:20:39.530 --> 00:20:41.780
You knew I would...

00:20:45.320 --> 00:20:49.950
Did you know Comrade Chief sent a threat?

00:20:49.950 --> 00:20:51.410
A threat?

00:20:51.410 --> 00:20:56.540
Yes. "If you kill Irina,
I'll kill the rocket."

00:20:56.540 --> 00:20:57.590
Chief...

00:20:57.590 --> 00:21:01.130
So much for treating her like an object.

00:21:01.130 --> 00:21:06.430
I moved exactly how
you wanted today, didn't I?

00:21:06.430 --> 00:21:07.600
Meaning?

00:21:07.600 --> 00:21:14.270
You wanted a revolutionary who
would lead us to the new world.

00:21:14.270 --> 00:21:15.440
I did.

00:21:15.440 --> 00:21:18.400
We're not pawns for your revolution!

00:21:20.480 --> 00:21:26.780
But, thank you for acknowledging me.
Now I can proudly go to the moon.

00:21:26.780 --> 00:21:31.370
You're serious?
It's 380,000 kilometers away.

00:21:31.370 --> 00:21:33.540
We'll go, for sure.

00:21:35.670 --> 00:21:39.380
Stay here until the
press conference, all right?

00:21:43.420 --> 00:21:45.800
"April 23rd"

00:21:45.800 --> 00:21:48.760
"April 23rd"
380,000 kilometers.

00:21:48.760 --> 00:21:52.020
"We'll make the impossible possible."

00:21:52.020 --> 00:21:57.150
The words of the 20th-century
scientist who pioneered rocketry.

00:21:57.150 --> 00:21:59.310
And it came true.

00:21:59.310 --> 00:22:04.650
For ages, people around the globe
have dreamed of going to the moon.

00:22:04.650 --> 00:22:08.660
We should all cooperate, even with the UK.

00:22:08.660 --> 00:22:11.030
You think it's possible?

00:22:11.030 --> 00:22:12.490
I do.

00:22:14.790 --> 00:22:20.710
Didn't you see it from space?
There are no borders to be seen...

00:22:20.710 --> 00:22:23.550
...on this blue, beautiful, planet.

00:23:00.790 --> 00:23:07.880
During the 21st century, I'm sure
lots of people will live in space--

00:23:07.880 --> 00:23:12.550
regardless of race or ethnicity.

00:23:13.600 --> 00:23:19.730
I believe that what we achieved
was a small step towards the future.

00:23:27.820 --> 00:23:30.610
Now, let's go...!

00:23:30.610 --> 00:23:32.820
...to our future!
